(4704170, 678287, 39679, '<td valign="top">This is actually a really nice shot but I can''t figure out why you decided to present it a angle.  The angle of the shot is an element of composition and, like any element, should be included only if it adds to the photo.  In this case, to me anyway, it doesn''t.</td>', 'This is actually a really nice shot but I can''t figure out why you decided to present it a angle.  The angle of the shot is an element of composition and, like any element, should be included only if it adds to the photo.  In this case, to me anyway, it doesn''t.', '2008-05-15 11:33:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4704174, 678391, 39679, '<td valign="top">Wow...that''s some serious saturation!  It''s a nice shot but many of your highlights are "blown out" and with such extreme saturation it''s particularly noticable.  I''d love to see this shot again with less harsh lighting.  I think you''d have a really excellent image.</td>', 'Wow...that''s some serious saturation!  It''s a nice shot but many of your highlights are "blown out" and with such extreme saturation it''s particularly noticable.  I''d love to see this shot again with less harsh lighting.  I think you''d have a really excellent image.', '2008-05-15 11:35:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4704177, 677428, 39679, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  We''re all told to not shoot images from "eye" level and your image is a good example of why this is good advice.</td>', 'Very nice.  We''re all told to not shoot images from "eye" level and your image is a good example of why this is good advice.', '2008-05-15 11:37:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(4704182, 677921, 39679, '<td valign="top">Really nice shot.  That said, the context, in your image, is such that it almost looks like there are windows on the ground.  I''m wondering if shooting it from the side, rather than below, would have been a better choice as you could more easily see that the bike was on the side of a building.  Just a thought but it really is a good shot.</td>', 'Really nice shot.  That said, the context, in your image, is such that it almost looks like there are windows on the ground.  I''m wondering if shooting it from the side, rather than below, would have been a better choice as you could more easily see that the bike was on the side of a building.  Just a thought but it really is a good shot.', '2008-05-15 11:40:26.000000', NULL, 1),
