(4714582, 677156, 61961, '<td valign="top">Found it!<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=648155" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49109/120/648155.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49109/120/648155.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/45000-49999/49109/120/648155.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I''m glad you were wrong about this being "too artsy" for a DPC challenge!  I think you''ve improved on the composition and I like the deeper colors, too.</td>', 'Found it!  I''m glad you were wrong about this being "too artsy" for a DPC challenge!  I think you''ve improved on the composition and I like the deeper colors, too.', '2008-05-21 10:10:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4714605, 678575, 48201, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  I knew the backdrop would be an issue, but had no time or $ to do better (no time even to iron the sheet).  I was actually outside, but there''s a stucco wall and window behind the sheet, so that wasn''t an option.  Being that I was shooting alone (that''s me on the bike), it was impossible to try to do a motion shot.  I''ve actually tried that before and it is impossible to get clipped in and pedaling nicely before the shutter releases.  The B&amp;W and posterization on my leg was intended.  The set up was the camera on the ground with a chair next to it to toss the shutter release onto once I got on the bike and clipped into the pedals.  The light is sun coming from almost directly behind me.<br/> <br/>I wish I had more time for challenges so I could do better, but you make do with what you have.  At least I learn things from this place.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  I knew the backdrop would be an issue, but had no time or $ to do better (no time even to iron the sheet).  I was actually outside, but there''s a stucco wall and window behind the sheet, so that wasn''t an option.  Being that I was shooting alone (that''s me on the bike), it was impossible to try to do a motion shot.  I''ve actually tried that before and it is impossible to get clipped in and pedaling nicely before the shutter releases.  The B&W and posterization on my leg was intended.  The set up was the camera on the ground with a chair next to it to toss the shutter release onto once I got on the bike and clipped into the pedals.  The light is sun coming from almost directly behind me. I wish I had more time for challenges so I could do better, but you make do with what you have.  At least I learn things from this place.', '2008-05-21 10:17:06.000000', NULL, 0),
