(4724060, 678194, 89065, '<td valign="top">peter! omg, this is wicked! and you said you just took a mediocre shot! holy shiza!<br/>congrats! &amp;hearts;</td>', 'peter! omg, this is wicked! and you said you just took a mediocre shot! holy shiza!congrats! &hearts;', '2008-05-26 04:35:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4724642, 677790, 68035, '<td valign="top">I would not have put this down as one of yours.  I have to say I LOVE the composition, especially the fact that the bright red of the cycle and cyclist adds to the sense of interloping.  I do find the light flare and slight central light haze a bit offputting, but the fact that this scored in the 3''s is quite frankly astonishing to me</td>', 'I would not have put this down as one of yours.  I have to say I LOVE the composition, especially the fact that the bright red of the cycle and cyclist adds to the sense of interloping.  I do find the light flare and slight central light haze a bit offputting, but the fact that this scored in the 3''s is quite frankly astonishing to me', '2008-05-26 11:12:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4725760, 678208, 24454, '<td valign="top">Well, DARN for the DQ!   I really love it.  And the big white border serves almost as part of the photo and enhances it beautifully.   I hate DQ''s.   Sometimes, I think it would be so cool if we could just submit our photos and not even have to answer to anyone about how we got the shot.   That''s how it is on other sites and I think it would actually work -- because generally the general public kills photos that cross the line anyway.<br/> <br/>Sigh.  I think this is an awesome photo.   Much more interesting than a straight up shot of a bicycle, right?  !</td>', 'Well, DARN for the DQ!   I really love it.  And the big white border serves almost as part of the photo and enhances it beautifully.   I hate DQ''s.   Sometimes, I think it would be so cool if we could just submit our photos and not even have to answer to anyone about how we got the shot.   That''s how it is on other sites and I think it would actually work -- because generally the general public kills photos that cross the line anyway. Sigh.  I think this is an awesome photo.   Much more interesting than a straight up shot of a bicycle, right?  !', '2008-05-26 18:57:59.000000', NULL, 0),
